{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Sleeve up there, I'll grab the pressure before the doctor is with you.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, I'm wrecked. Can we not drag this out.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): One forty eight over ninety two. Pulse is seventy six.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He legged it over from the site, the bus was late. That'll have it up.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (NURSE): Mm. My own sister is the very same, forever checking. She's on metformin for the sugar and she gives out about it non-stop.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Look, I don't want your sister's story. I've a lump in me groin.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (DOCTOR): Doctor Keane. Which side.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Right. It comes up when I'm lifting the blocks and it goes away once I lie down.",
  "[SEG0009] person_4 (DOCTOR): How long.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm. A few weeks. Maybe 6. I haven't a clue, I'm not counting.",
  "[SEG0011] person_4 (DOCTOR): Sore.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really pain. A mild ache come the evening, after the shift.",
  "[SEG0013] person_4 (DOCTOR): Vomiting.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (DOCTOR): Nausea.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (DOCTOR): Bowels changed.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0019] person_4 (DOCTOR): Fever or sweats.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He has the blood pressure as well, tell the doctor.",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (DOCTOR): High blood pressure. Yes or no.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. Five-ish years. I'm on the amladipine.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (DOCTOR): Dose.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Err, ten... no. Five milligram. One in the morning.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He does miss it some mornings if he's flying out the door.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): I do not. I take it. Don't be saying that.",
  "[SEG0028] person_4 (DOCTOR): Headaches with it.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. End of the day. Not every day like.",
  "[SEG0030] person_4 (DOCTOR): Chest pain.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (DOCTOR): Short of breath.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0034] person_4 (DOCTOR): Any drug allergies.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): His sister gets biotin for her hair, that's her own yoke, nothing to do with him.",
  "[SEG0037] person_4 (DOCTOR): Lie flat. Cough for me. And again.",
  "[SEG0038] person_4 (DOCTOR): Soft lump in the right groin. It slips back lying down and the cough pushes it out.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Right, so what is it. I want to get home, I'm done in.",
  "[SEG0040] person_4 (DOCTOR): It's a hernia. A bit of bowel is pushing through a weak spot in the muscle wall there. Lifting shoves it out, lying down lets it fall back.",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): His father had a hernia operation, years ago now.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Can they not just sort it today.",
  "[SEG0043] person_4 (DOCTOR): No. I'll refer you to the surgeons and they'll see you about a repair.",
  "[SEG0044] person_4 (DOCTOR): No heavy lifting until they've seen you. If a lift has to be done, get a second pair of hands on it. If the lump will not go back in or you start vomiting, come back the same day.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (PATIENT): Fine. Grand.",
  "[SEG0046] person_1 (NURSE): I'll get that referral typed. There's tea in the waiting room if you want it, the machine is acting up though."
 ],
